Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:35:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 139/148] fix(polecat): test live-owner ownership against the
 session's identity set (gcp-fooz4)

0085 decided "the work bead is someone else's" with one string compare,
GUARD_OWNER != EXPECTED_ASSIGNEE. One session answers to several
spellings: gc 1.4.3 recorded claims under the runtime session_name, and a
gc 1.5.0 namepool polecat acts under its alias (BEADS_ACTOR =
session.AssigneeIdentifier). A molecule that straddles the upgrade finds
its own work bead under the old spelling, the liveness probe finds that
spelling's live row, which is this session, and the guard declines its own
molecule.

The guard now treats the owner as this session when it equals any of
BEADS_ACTOR, GC_ALIAS, GC_SESSION_ID, GC_SESSION_NAME or GC_AGENT. That is
upstream #360's identity-set fix for the claim (9f98ea4e,
claim_assignee_is_ours in gascity/commands/claim/run.sh), carried here as
the same function. A self match skips the liveness probe and goes to the
takeover from the previous commit, which moves the bead to the spelling
bd checks writes against, so step 6's handoff is not refused either.

Test: test_polecat_live_owner_guard.sh
test_own_molecule_under_another_spelling_is_not_declined (owner
gastown__polecat-gc-psfm, EXPECTED_ASSIGNEE winnow/gastown.nux, both this
session). Red before: "CLAIM_DECLINED_LIVE_OWNER ... that owner is live
(session gc-psfm)". Green after. The harness now resets BEADS_ACTOR and the
GC_* identity variables so the runner's own session cannot leak in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
